DTEND:20261023T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:National Chemistry Week is joining forces with Open Access Week to feature open-access resources in chemistry!\n\nGet ready to go full mole! We're throwing a high-energy bash in honor of the quirkiest number in chemistry—Avogadro’s number (6.022 × 10²³)—and you're invited to join the reaction!\n\nExplosive fun for all! Whether you're a chemistry whiz or just here for the vibes\, this celebration is bound to be elemental.\n\nGames! Treats! Prizes! No registration needed—show up and dive in!\n\nFind us behind the turnstiles at Dirac Science Library. Let’s make this Mole Day unforgettable!
GEO:30.44502;-84.299845
LOCATION:Dirac Science Library (DSL)\, main floor\, behind turnstiles
SUMMARY:Mole Day Madness
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/mole-day-madness-Fall2026
CATEGORIES:Tabling
END:VEVENT
