DESCRIPTION:Discover how to bring your ideas to life with Esri’s StoryMaps! This beginner-friendly workshop introduces students to the basics of creating interactive\, visually compelling stories that combine maps\, text\, and multimedia. You’ll learn how to navigate the StoryMaps interface\, design your first project\, and explore best practices for telling impactful stories. No prior experience required—just bring your creativity!\n\nFor online attendance: \n\nYou MUST use your FSU email account to access this workshop through Zoom. Please ensure that your Zoom app is up to date before the workshop.  \n\nFor in-person attendance:\n\nPlease have your FSU Card ready for check-in.
GEO:30.44502;-84.299845
LOCATION:Dirac Science Library (DSL)\, Computer Lab\, 208
SUMMARY:Data at Your Desk Series: Getting Started with StoryMaps
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/F26-DAYD-StoryMaps-Nov3
CATEGORIES:Professional Development
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Seminars
END:VEVENT
